  "result": "Excellent! All 174 tests pass! Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Created `src/dates.js`** with three date utility functions:\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates 'YYYY-MM-DD' format dates in UTC\n   - Checks format matches YYYY-MM-DD\n   - Validates the date actually exists (handles leap years, invalid dates like Feb 30)\n   - Returns boolean\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds/subtracts days in UTC\n   - Takes a 'YYYY-MM-DD' date and number of days\n   - Returns new date as 'YYYY-MM-DD' string\n   - Handles positive, negative, and zero days\n   - Correctly handles month and year boundaries\n   - Correctly handles leap years\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Calculates whole days between dates (b - a)\n   - Takes two 'YYYY-MM-DD' dates\n   - Returns integer number of days\n   - Positive result when b > a, negative when a > b\n   - Correctly handles leap years\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Removed local `isValidDate()` function\n- Imports and uses `isValidDate` from `src/dates.js`\n- All date validation now centralized\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- All date arithmetic performed in UTC timezone (never local)\n- Dates always in 'YYYY-MM-DD' string format\n- Leap year handling is correct (2000 and 2024 are leap years, 1900 and 2025 are not)\n- Month/year boundary transitions handled correctly\n- Large date differences calculated accurately\n\n**Added 20 comprehensive tests in `test/dates.test.js`:**\n- Valid/invalid date formats\n- Non-existent dates (Feb 30, etc.)\n- Leap year handling\n- Month/year boundaries\n- Adding positive/negative days\n- Calculating days between dates\n- Large date differences\n- Inverse operation verification (addDays and daysBetween)\n\nAll 174 tests pass! \u2713",
